{
  "state": {
    "case_id": "220",
    "case_summary": "An HIV-negative man presented with a 12-month history of left-sided nasal congestion and obstruction despite medical treatment.\n\nPhysical examination revealed a large polypoid mass obstructing the left nasal cavity.\n\n- Imaging Studies:    1. Computed Tomographic Imaging:       Image Title: Computed Tomographic Images Demonstrating Soft Tissue Mass       Image Description: Soft tissue polypoid density not involving the orbit or skull base, obstructing the left nasal cavity        2. Pathological Analysis:       - CD138-positive       - CD56-positive       - CD20-negative       - PAX5-negative       - EBV-positive       - Fluorescence in situ hybridization showed gains of florescence signal at multiple loci:         * 3q27 (BCL6)         * 8q24 (MYC)         * 14q32 (IGH)        3. Additional Studies:       - MRI       - PET scan       - Bone marrow biopsy       (All showed no local or distant metastatic disease)\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Extramedullary plasmacytoma\nB. Non-Hodgkin lymphoma, not otherwise specified\nC. Primary extramedullary plasmacytoma\nD. Plasmablastic lymphoma (PBL), stage 1 with high-risk features\n",
